hadiths[115]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! We travel by sea and carry only a little water with us. If we use that water for ablution, we will be left thirsty. So can we perform ablution with the sea water?"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) replied: ""Its water is pure and its dead (animals) are lawful."
"2","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: ""Indeed, pieces of meat from dogs and cloths stained with menstrual blood are thrown into the well of Budā‘ah (the name of a well). (Can we attain purification with its water?)"" So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Nothing makes water impure."
"3","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should urinate in standing water and then perform ghusl with it."
"4","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When water reaches the amount of two large pitchers, it does not accept impurity or filth."
"5","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When the amount of water reaches the equivalent of two large pitchers, it does not accept impurity."" In this hadith, there is an explanation of the pitchers of the place called Hajar. Ibn Jurayj said: ""I have seen the pitchers of the place Hajar; one pitcher is equal to two leather water-skins or two and a little more of water."
"6","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) was asked: ""Can we perform ablution with water left by donkeys?"" He (ﷺ) replied: ""Yes, and also with water left by any kind of wild beasts."
"7","Kabshah bint Ka'b bin Malik, who was the wife of Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) or one of his sons, narrates: Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) came, so I placed a vessel for his ablution. A cat came and drank water from that vessel. She says: Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) saw me looking at it with astonishment, so he said: ""Are you astonished, O my niece? Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'It is not impure. It is among those (creatures) that go around among you.'"
"8","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a dog drinks from the vessel of any one of you, he should wash it seven times."
"9","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a dog licks the utensil of any one of you, he should wash it seven times."
"10","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a dog licks the utensil of any one of you, he should wash it seven times. The first time or the last time with soil."
"11","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would perform ghusl with a ""farq"" (a specific measure of water). And I and the Prophet (peace be upon him) would perform ghusl from the same vessel."
"12","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she says: ""The Prophet (ﷺ) and I used to bathe from the same vessel."
"13","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she says: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and I used to perform ghusl from the same vessel, and sometimes I would say to him: Leave some water for me, leave some water for me."
"14","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he narrates from Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she and the Prophet (ﷺ) used to perform ghusl from the same vessel."
"15","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: ""In the time of the Prophet ﷺ, men and women used to perform ablution together."
"16","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when the time for Asr prayer had come, and the people searched for water. When they did not find any water, water for ablution was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a vessel. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) put his hand in it and instructed the people to perform ablution from that (vessel). Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I saw water gushing forth from beneath his (peace and blessings be upon him) fingers, and the people performed ablution until even the last person (in the caravan) had performed ablution."
"17","Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead goat which he ﷺ had given to the freed slave woman of Umm al-Mu’minin Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her). He ﷺ said: “Why did you not benefit from its skin?” The people said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! It is dead. He ﷺ said: “Only its eating has been forbidden.”"
"18","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) heard the Prophet ﷺ saying: ""Any hide that is tanned becomes pure."
"19","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) instructed to benefit from the hide of a dead animal after tanning it."
"20","It is narrated from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever drinks from silver vessels is pouring the fire of Hell into his belly."
"21","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A Bedouin urinated in the mosque. The people rushed towards him, but the Prophet (ﷺ) stopped the people and said: ""Pour a bucket of water over the urine."
"22","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he states: A Bedouin entered the mosque and said, ""O Allah! Have mercy on Muhammad (ﷺ) and me, and do not have mercy on anyone else besides us."" (Hearing this) the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""You have limited (Allah's) vast mercy."" Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: After a short while, he urinated in a corner of the mosque and the people hurried to stop him. But the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stopped them, then ordered a bucket or tub of water, which was poured over the urine. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Teach and be gentle, do not be harsh."
"23","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that I used to scrape semen off the garment of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)."
"24","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that I used to scrape semen off the garment of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)."
"25","Narrated by Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: I used to scrape semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), then he (ﷺ) would wear that same garment and pray."
"26","Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding semen that gets on clothes, said: ""Remove it with a piece of wood or grass, because it is like saliva or nasal discharge."
"27","Mus'ab bin Sa'd narrates that when semen would get on Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas's (may Allah be pleased with him) clothes, if it was wet, he would clean it, and if it was dry, he would rub the clothes, and then he would pray in them."
"28","It is narrated from Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her), she states: I asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about menstrual blood that gets on a garment. He (ﷺ) said: ""Scrape it off, then rub it with water, then wash it with water, and then pray in it."
"29","Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I asked the Prophet ﷺ about menstrual blood, and the rest of the hadith is as in the previous narration."
"30","Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: A woman asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, ""If menstrual blood gets on any of our clothes, what do you think she should do?"" The Prophet ﷺ replied: ""If menstrual blood gets on any of your clothes, she should rub it and wash it with water, then pour clean water over it, and then she may pray in it."
"31","It is narrated from the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Prophet ﷺ was asked about a garment that had menstrual blood on it. He ﷺ said: ""First, scrape it off, then rub it with water and wash it, then pray in it."
"32","It is narrated from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that a woman asked Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her): ""My garment is long and I walk on dirty places."" Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) replied that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The earth that comes after purifies it."
"33","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am like a father to you. When any of you goes to relieve himself, he should neither face the Qiblah nor turn his back towards it, and he commanded to perform istinja with three stones, and forbade using dung and bones for istinja, and forbade a man from performing istinja with his right hand."
"34","Khuzaymah bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (ﷺ) said regarding istinja: ""It is with three stones, in which there is neither dung nor manure."
"35","It is narrated from Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade us from facing the Qiblah when relieving ourselves, but instructed us to face either the east or the west. Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) says: When we went to Syria, we saw that the places built for urination were facing the Qiblah, so we returned seeking forgiveness from Allah."
"36","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: ""Some people say that when you sit to relieve yourself, your face should not be towards the Qiblah or Bayt al-Maqdis."" Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""I climbed onto the roof of my house and I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sitting on two bricks, facing Bayt al-Maqdis to relieve himself."
"37","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man passed by the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was urinating. The man greeted the Prophet (ﷺ) with salam, and the Prophet (ﷺ) replied to him. When the man went away, the Prophet (ﷺ) called him back and said: ""I replied to your salam only so that you would not say that I greeted the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he did not reply to me. When you see me in this state again, do not greet me with salam. If you do, I will not reply to you."
"38","It is narrated from Ibn Sammah (may Allah be pleased with him) who says: I passed by the Prophet ﷺ while he was urinating. I greeted him with salam, but he did not reply to me until he stood by a wall and scratched it with a stick that he had with him. Then he struck his hand on the wall, wiped his face and hands, and then replied to my salam."
"39","It is narrated from Ibn Sammah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) urinated and then performed tayammum."
"40","It is narrated from Sulaiman bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) went towards Bi’r-e-Jamal to relieve himself. When he returned, a man greeted him with salam, but he did not reply until he wiped his hand on the wall, then he returned the greeting."
"41","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you wakes up from sleep, he should wash his hands three times before putting them into a vessel, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"42","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any one of you wakes up from sleep, he should wash his hands before putting them into the vessel for ablution, for none of you knows where his hand spent the night."
"43","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""When any of you wakes up from sleep, he should wash his hands before putting them into the vessel for ablution, because none of you knows where his hand spent the night."
"44","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you wakes up from sleep, he should wash his hands before putting them into the vessel for ablution, because he does not know where his hands spent the night."
"45","Yahya al-Mazini (may Allah have mercy on him) said to Abdullah bin Zayd al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Can you show me how the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed ablution?"" Abdullah bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: ""Yes,"" then he called for water for ablution, poured it on his hands and washed his hands twice, rinsed his mouth and put water into his nose three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his hands up to and including the elbows twice, then wiped his head with both hands, moving his hands from the front to the back and then from the back to the front. He started from the beginning of the head, then took both hands to the nape, then brought them back to where he had started while wiping, then washed both his feet."
"46","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed ablution, he washed his face three times, and washed his hands twice each, and wiped his head with his hands such that he moved both hands from the front of the head to the back, and then brought them from the back to the front. He started from the front part of the head and took his hands to the nape, and then in the same way brought both hands back to the place from where he had started wiping. Then he washed both his feet."
"47","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution, put his hand into the vessel, rinsed his nose and mouth once, then put his hand in again and washed his face once, and washed his hands once, and wiped his head and ears once."
"48","Mughira bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Prophet (ﷺ) performed ablution, he wiped over his forehead, turban, and socks."
"49","Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ablution, removed his turban, and wiped over the front part of his head, or said that he wiped his forehead with water."
"50","Mughira bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wiped his forehead or said that he wiped the front part of his head with water."
"51","It is narrated from Laqeet bin Sabrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he says: I was among the delegation of Banu Al-Muntafiq. We came to the Prophet ﷺ but could not meet him. We encountered Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), so she sent us dates in a vessel made of palm leaves and ordered that small pieces of meat be cooked for us. The meat was cooked, and then we ate. We stayed for a while, and then the Prophet ﷺ also arrived. He said: “Have you eaten anything? Was anything brought for you?” We said: Yes. After a short while, a shepherd drove some goats, and among them, one goat was crying. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O so-and-so! What has the goat given birth to?” The shepherd said: “A kid.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Slaughter a goat in its place for us.” Then the Prophet ﷺ turned to me and said: “Do not think that we slaughtered this animal for you. We have a hundred goats; we do not want them to increase. When one goat gives birth, we slaughter another in its place.” Laqeet bin Sabrah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! My wife has a bad tongue. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Divorce her.” I said: I have spent time with her and I have children from her. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Advise her; if there is good in her, she will accept it. And do not beat your wife like a slave-girl.” I said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Tell me about ablution (wudu)? The Prophet ﷺ said: “Perform ablution thoroughly, pass your fingers between the fingers, and rinse your nose well except when you are fasting.”"
"52","Salim (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that we set out for Makkah with Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), and she used to set out with my father and also used to pray with him. Salim says that water for ablution was brought for Abdur Rahman bin Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), so Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Abdur Rahman, complete the ablution thoroughly. I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: ""Woe to the heels from the fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"53","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said to her (brother) Abdur Rahman: O Abdur Rahman, perform ablution thoroughly! I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: ""Woe to the heels from the fire."
"54","Humran (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) performed ablution at his sitting place and washed each limb of ablution three times, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: “Whoever performs ablution like this of mine, his sins will depart from his face, hands, and feet.”"
"55","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I did not fear hardship and difficulty for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to delay the ‘Isha prayer and to use the miswak with every prayer."
"56","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The miswak purifies the mouth and is a means of the Lord's pleasure."
"57","Urwah bin Zubair (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: I went to Marwan bin Hakam and we discussed what things make ablution (wudu) necessary. Marwan said: Touching the private part makes ablution necessary. Urwah said: I do not know about this. Marwan said: Basrah bint Safwan (may Allah be pleased with her) informed me that she heard the Prophet ﷺ saying: ""When any one of you touches his private part, he should perform ablution."
"58","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he reports from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""When any one of you touches his private part with his hand while there is nothing (such as cloth, etc.) in between, then he should perform ablution."
"59","Muhammad bin Abdur Rahman bin Thawban reports that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When any one of you touches his private part, he should perform ablution."
"60","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: ""When a woman touches her private part, she should perform ablution."
"61","Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that a husband kissing his wife and touching her is considered an act of touching, therefore whoever kisses his wife or touches her, ablution becomes obligatory upon him."
"62","It is narrated from Miqdad bin Aswad (may Allah be pleased with him) that Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) told him to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about a man who approaches his wife and pre-seminal fluid (madhiy) is discharged—what should he do? Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) is (married) to me, and I feel shy to ask. Miqdad (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about this, and he said: ""When any of you experiences this, he should wash his private part and perform ablution as he does for prayer."
"63","Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that when Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would have a nosebleed, he would leave the prayer, perform ablution, and return without speaking."
"64","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: ""Whoever has a nosebleed, or experiences madhiy (pre-seminal fluid), or vomits, should go back and perform ablution, and then return to the same place and resume the prayer from there."
"65","Abdullah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that it was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him): ""If a person has a thought of losing his ablution during prayer (what should he do)?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""He should not turn back (i.e., break his prayer) unless he hears a sound or perceives a smell."
"66","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would wait for the ‘Isha prayer, and due to overpowering sleep, their heads would droop while sitting, but they would perform the prayer without renewing their ablution."
"67","Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would fall asleep while sitting, then perform prayer and would not perform ablution."
"68","Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""Whoever sleeps lying down, wudu becomes obligatory upon him, and whoever sleeps sitting, there is no wudu upon him."
"69","It is narrated from Amr bin Umayyah Damri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ate the meat of a goat’s shoulder and performed prayer without renewing ablution."
"70","Ibn Shihab (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered the person who laughed during prayer to repeat his ablution and prayer."
"71","Hasan al-Basri (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates, similar to the previous hadith from the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"72","It is narrated from Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with them both), he says: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) entered and went for some need (to relieve themselves), then both came out. Usama says: I asked Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him): What did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) do? Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: He went to relieve himself, then performed ablution, so he washed his face and hands, wiped his head, and wiped over his socks (as well)."
"73","Urwah bin Mughirah narrates that Mughira bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) informed him that he participated in the Battle of Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Mughira says: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to relieve himself before Fajr, and I was carrying a water vessel with him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, I began pouring water from the vessel over his hands. He ﷺ washed his hands three times, then washed his face, then tried to remove his cloak from his arms, but the sleeves of the cloak were tight, so he inserted his hands into the cloak and brought them out from underneath, and washed his arms up to and including the elbows, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, then returned. Mughira says: I also turned back with him. We saw that the people were praying under the leadership of Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet ﷺ prayed one rak’ah with the congregation and the second rak’ah separately with the people. When Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) finished the prayer with salam, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and completed his prayer. This incident worried the Muslims and they began to say “Subhan Allah” repeatedly. When the Prophet ﷺ completed the prayer, he turned to the companions and said: “You did well,” or he said, “You did right.” It was as if he ﷺ was encouraging them to pray on time."
"74","Mughira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I intended to move Abdur Rahman (bin Awf) back, but the Prophet ﷺ said to me, ""Leave him."
"75","It is narrated from Mughira bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him), he states: I said, “O Messenger of Allah! Can we wipe over the leather socks?” He ﷺ said: “Yes, provided you put them on while in a state of ablution.”"
"76","Mughira bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out to relieve himself during the expedition of Tabuk, then (afterwards) he performed ablution, wiped over his leather socks, and offered prayer."
"77","Nafi' and Abdullah bin Dinar narrate that when Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) went to Kufa, Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) was the governor there. He saw that Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) was wiping over his leather socks, so Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) objected to him. Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Ask your father."" Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) asked, and Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""When you put on the leather socks in a state of ablution, then wipe over them."" Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) asked: ""What if we go to relieve ourselves?"" Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Even if you go to relieve yourself, (still wipe over them)."
"78","Nafi' narrates that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) urinated in the marketplace, then performed ablution and wiped over his socks, then offered prayer."
"79","Saeed bin Abdur Rahman bin Ruqaish says: I saw Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) come to Quba (village), he urinated and performed ablution, then wiped over his leather socks and (afterwards) offered prayer."
"80","Abd Khair narrates that Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) wiped over the upper part of his feet while performing ablution and said: ""If I had not seen the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wiping over the upper part of the feet, I would have thought that the lower part is better (to wipe over)."
"81","Nafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) performed ablution in the market, washed his face and hands, then wiped over his head. Then he was called for a funeral prayer. When he entered the mosque to perform the funeral prayer, he wiped over his socks, and then performed the funeral prayer."
"82","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) that it is narrated from Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he urinated in the market, then washed his face and hands, then wiped over his head, then entered the mosque. He was called for a funeral prayer, so he wiped over his leather socks and performed the funeral prayer. It is permissible to wipe over socks as well as leather socks."
"83","It is narrated from Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) granted concession to the traveler to wipe over the leather socks for three days and three nights, and to the resident for one day and one night."
"84","It is narrated from Zir bin Hubaish (may Allah have mercy on him), he says: I presented myself before Safwan bin Assal Al-Muradi (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said: ""For what purpose have you come?"" He says: I said, ""For the acquisition of knowledge."" So he said: ""The angels spread their wings for the seeker of knowledge, being pleased with what he seeks."" I said: ""After urination and defecation, I have some doubt in my heart regarding wiping over the socks, while you are among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I have come to ask you whether you have heard anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about this?"" Safwan bin Assal (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Yes! When we were on a journey or were travelers, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to command us not to remove our socks for three days and three nights except in the case of major impurity (janabah), but not after urination, defecation, or sleep (there is no need to remove the socks)."
"85","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she says: We were on a journey with the Prophet (ﷺ) when my necklace broke (got lost), so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stayed to look for it, while the people of the caravan had no water with them, so the verse of tayammum was revealed."
"86","Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We performed tayammum up to the shoulders with the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"87","It is narrated from Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him), he says: We were on a journey with the Prophet (ﷺ) when the verse of tayammum was revealed, so we performed tayammum up to the shoulders with the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"88","Ibn Sammah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I passed by the Prophet ﷺ while he was urinating. (After finishing,) he touched the wall, then performed tayammum on his face and arms."
"89","Ibn Sammah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wiped his face and hands in tayammum."
"90","Nafi' narrates from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that he came from the place of Juruf, and when he reached near the (camel) enclosure, he performed tayammum, wiped his face and hands, and offered the Asr prayer. Then he entered Madinah while the sun was still high, and he did not repeat the prayer."
"91","It is narrated from Nafi‘ that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) performed tayammum near the enclosure of cattle and offered the ‘Asr prayer. Then he entered Madinah while the sun was still high, but he did not repeat the prayer."
"92","Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered a person in the state of janabah to perform tayammum, then offer prayer, and when water becomes available, he should perform ghusl. In the narration from Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), it is stated: ""When you find water, then perform ghusl with it."
"93","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of Abu Talhah, came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! Allah is not shy of the truth. Is it obligatory for a woman to perform ghusl when she has a wet dream?"" He replied: ""Yes, when she sees the fluid."
"94","It is narrated from Zubayd bin Salat that he reports: I went with Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) towards Juruf. He saw that he had experienced a wet dream and had performed the prayer without taking a bath. So he said: ""By Allah, I do not know that I was in a state of janabah, and I did not take a bath and performed the prayer."" Zubayd says: He then took a bath and washed the part of the garment where semen was visible, and where it was not visible, he sprinkled water. He gave the adhan and iqamah, and after the sun had risen high, he performed the prayer."
"95","It is narrated from Sa'id bin Al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: ""The difference of opinion among the companions of Muhammad ﷺ on an issue has become burdensome for me, and I consider it important to present it before you."" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""What is that issue? Why do you not want to ask your mother about it? Ask me!"" So Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): ""A man goes to his wife and withdraws before ejaculation."" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""When the circumcised part passes the circumcised part, ghusl becomes obligatory."" Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""After you, I will never ask anyone (about this issue) ever again."
"96","It is narrated from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) asked Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) about the meeting of the two circumcised parts, so Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When the two circumcised parts (private parts) meet, or when the circumcised part touches the circumcised part, then ghusl becomes obligatory."
"97","Narrated by Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""When any of you sits between the four branches and then joins the private part with the woman's private part, then ghusl becomes obligatory."
"98","Narrated by Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl becomes obligatory. I and the Prophet (ﷺ) did this act and (afterwards) we performed ghusl."
"99","It is narrated from Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him), he states: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! When one of us has intercourse and withdraws before ejaculation, what should he do?"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""He should wash the part that touched the woman, then perform ablution and then offer prayer."
"100","It is narrated from Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to say: Whoever has not ejaculated, ghusl is not obligatory upon him. Then, before his death, Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) retracted from this statement."
"101","It is narrated from Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: In the beginning of Islam, the use of water (i.e., performing ghusl) was required only upon the emission of semen, but later this was abandoned, and the command for ghusl was given merely upon the joining of the private parts."
"102","It is narrated from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he says: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! May my parents be sacrificed for you, indeed my father has passed away."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Go and bury him in the ground."" I said, ""He died in a state of polytheism."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Go and bury him in the ground."" When I had buried him in the ground and came to the Prophet (ﷺ), he said, ""Go and take a bath."
"103","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed ghusl after janabah, he would first wash his hands, then perform wudu as for prayer, then insert his fingers into the water and run them through the roots of his hair, then pour three handfuls of water over his head with his hands, and then pour water over his entire body."
"104","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) intended to perform ghusl after janabah, he would wash his hands before putting them into the vessel, then wash his private parts, then perform wudu as for prayer, then wet his hair with water, then pour three handfuls of water over his head."
"105","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (ﷺ) would pour three handfuls (of water) over his head when he was in a state of janabah."
"106","It is narrated from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! I braid my hair, should I undo them when performing ghusl (ritual bath) after impurity?"" He (ﷺ) replied: ""No (there is no need to undo them), it is sufficient for you to pour three handfuls of water over your head, then pour water over the rest of your body, and you will be purified."
"107","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she says: A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the ritual bath after menstruation. The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Take a piece of cotton with musk and purify yourself with it."" The woman asked: ""How should I purify myself with it?"" The Prophet ﷺ replied: ""Purify yourself with it."" She asked: ""How should I purify myself with it?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Subhan Allah! Subhan Allah!"" and covered himself with a cloth, [saying] ""Purify yourself with it."" (Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, says) I pulled her towards me and understood what the Prophet ﷺ meant, then I said to her: ""Wipe it over the place where the blood was."
"108","It is narrated from the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), that during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a woman used to experience excessive bleeding. Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about her issue, so he ﷺ said: ""Estimate the number of nights and days she used to have menstruation before this illness of istihada, and leave prayers for that many days in the month. When that time passes, she should perform ghusl, then tie a cloth and perform the prayers."
"109","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that Fatimah bint Abi Hubaish said to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): ""I do not become pure (from bleeding), should I stop praying?"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""This is only a vein, it is not menstruation. When the days of menstruation come, stop praying, and when those days end, clean the blood from your body and pray."
"110","Hamnah bint Jahsh narrates that I used to have excessive bleeding (istihada). I came to the Prophet ﷺ to seek a religious ruling and found him at the house of his sister Zainab. I said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have something to ask you, it is something that I must ask but I also feel shy.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “What is it?” Hamnah said, “I have a severe complaint of istihada. What do you say about it? Because of this affliction, I am unable to perform prayer and fasting.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “I suggest you use cotton, for it absorbs the blood.” She said, “It is more than that.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Tie a cloth around yourself.” She said, “It is even more than that.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Use a piece of cloth.” She said, “It is even more than that (i.e., it does not stop, it keeps flowing).” The Prophet ﷺ said, “I command you with two things; whichever you do is correct. And if you are able to do both, then you know best.” Then the Prophet ﷺ said, “This is one of the kicks of Satan. Relying on Allah’s knowledge, consider yourself menstruating for six or seven days, then perform ghusl (ritual bath), and when you think you have become pure (from menstruation), then pray and fast for twenty-four days and nights or twenty-three prayers, and do so every month as women do in their fixed times of menstruation and purity.”"
"111","The wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), narrates that during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, a woman used to experience excessive bleeding. Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about her issue, so he ﷺ said: ""She should consider the number of nights and days in a month during which she used to have her menstrual period before this illness of istihada, and leave the prayer for that many days in the month. When that time passes, she should perform ghusl, tie a cloth (to stop the blood), and then perform the prayer."
"112","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that Umm Habibah bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her) suffered from istihada (non-menstrual bleeding) for seven years. She asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: ""This is a vein, not menstruation."" And he instructed her to perform ghusl and pray, so she would perform ghusl for every prayer. She would sit in a tub for ghusl, and the redness of the blood would appear on the water."
"113","It is narrated from Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: ""The duration of a woman's menstruation is from three or four (days) up to ten."
"114","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), and she mentioned being in the state of Ihram with the Prophet (ﷺ), that she experienced menstruation during that time. The Prophet (ﷺ) instructed her to do all the acts that pilgrims do except for the circumambulation of the House (Ka'bah) and prayer, until she became pure."
"115","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: I came to Makkah while I was menstruating. I neither performed the Tawaf of the House (Ka'bah) nor the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah. I asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about this, and he said: ""Do what the pilgrims do, except for the Tawaf of the House, until you become pure."
